03

Data preparation

A PySpark quality-audit and cleansing pipeline turned a messy 1.4 GB CSV into an analysis-ready Parquet file.

1

Audit No duplicates found; verified 7,079,079 rows × 37 columns.

2

Clean Removed negative scheduled times; standardised cancellation_code to 'Not Cancelled'.

3

Engineer Added is_delayed (15-min rule) and dep_time_block (Morning/Afternoon/Evening/Overnight).

4

Optimise Reordered, consolidated and exported one compressed Parquet file.

8× smaller. Columnar Parquet lets Spark read only the 18–26 columns each job needs, cutting I/O versus row-based CSV.

