07

Case study — the July 2024 CrowdStrike collapse

The data itself proves this was an IT/carrier failure, not weather — the smoking gun is in the causes.

Before (1–18 Jul)

Carrier delay 7.3 min · 22.4% delayed · few cancellations.

Outage (19–25 Jul)

Carrier delay jumps to 66 min; delay rate >53%; crew-tracking systems down.

Peak (21 Jul)

1,450+ cancellations in a day; 5,000+ over the week — system-wide gridlock.

Recovery (26–31 Jul)

IT restored: carrier delay back to ~7.6 min, cancellations near zero.

Weather delay stayed near 0 throughout — a single faulty software update, not the weather, drove the meltdown (Sigalos, 2024).

